        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0c89f1f7-19e5-5109-bcdc-bedbbbb43f05",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Singapore, North America, South Korea\n- Buildings: Tanjong Pagar Centre, One Raffles Place, UOB Plaza, Republic Plaza, 63 Building, Bank of China Tower\n- Topics: tallest buildings, height records\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, One Raffles Place was completed at 280 m and was the tallest building in the world outside North America at that time.\n- In 1986, One Raffles Place surpassed South Korea's 63 Building, which had been completed one year earlier.\n- One Raffles Place later lost its status as the tallest building outside North America to the Bank of China Tower.\n- For over 20 years, UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, and Republic Plaza jointly held the record for the tallest building in Singapore.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre has a height of 290 m.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre is currently the tallest building in Singapore.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre broke the previous Singapore height record that had been jointly held by UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, and Republic Plaza.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
